1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,504
Every minute you waste online steals breath straight from someone you love. You just refuse to believe it.

2
00:00:06,804 --> 00:00:15,564
Leo ignored the strange warning app on his phone until his grandmother suddenly collapsed into deep, silent sleep.

3
00:00:15,864 --> 00:00:24,648
The hospital room smelled like cold antiseptic. Machines beeped a steady, terrifying rhythm that mocked his deep panic.

4
00:00:24,948 --> 00:00:31,620
He pulled out his phone out of pure habit, opening his favorite social app to numb the sharp pain.

5
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:40,992
Instantly, the heart monitor beside the bed spiked. The flat line threatened to become a permanent, devastating reality.

6
00:00:41,292 --> 00:00:48,924
He locked the phone screen. The frantic beeping slowed back down to a steady, cautious, fragile rhythm.

7
00:00:49,224 --> 00:00:57,648
Curiosity poisoned his mind. He opened a video, watching the monitor drop flat the exact second playback started.

8
00:00:57,948 --> 00:01:06,204
He wasn't consuming content. He was consuming her remaining time on Earth, one mindless scroll at a time.

9
00:01:06,504 --> 00:01:14,400
Leo dropped the glowing device on the tile floor, rushing forward to finally look at the fragile face.

10
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:21,612
The wrinkled face on the pillow wasn't his grandmother at all. It was his own face, decades older.
